      "created_at": "2018-10-14T09:43:06Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-14T09:43:06Z",
      "body": "> \r\n> \r\n> A 1st view point... it is required to place on the -Contact Us- page a checkbox that the customer agree to the Privacy Policy before he can send a message.\r\n> ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10166095/46895227-25327680-ce80-11e8-8dac-5806944497bd.png)\r\n\r\nNot really true, because if someone contacts you (via Contact Us Page), the visitor is doing an action on his own behalf.\r\nThere are many discussions about adding a checkbox to a form (like this), some of them say yes, most of them say no.\r\nThe more, because the standard contact form in OpenCart has no further actions combined (e.g. answering through the system, or assigning it to an order, or doing more like in a CRM).\r\n\r\nAnd finally, \r\n1. IF there would be a checkbox, the consent has to be stored! \r\n2. And the customer/visitor should be able to withdraw his consent.\r\n\r\nGeneral: a contact form is something every visitor should know that further actions are done electronically.\r\nNo more consent is required.\r\n\r\nMore helpfully would be an additional text (with link) what this form can be used for - and the link points to the Privacy Statement.\r\n\r\nSee also Article 6 GDPR\r\n\r\nBut (!), if the contact form would have required fields like phone number, company name etc. > then a Checkbox is required.\r\nEverything else is stupid and nonsens!\r\n\r\nSample articles: https://www.webcellent.com/blog/eu-dsgvo-datenschutz-checkbox-pflicht-fuer-kontaktformulare/\r\nhttps://www.datenschutz-janolaw.de/info-faq/informationen/dsgvo/einwilligung.html\r\nhttps://www.datenschutz-guru.de/braucht-mein-kontaktformular-jetzt-eine-checkbox/ (Podcast around 6:00)",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/opencart/opencart/issues/comments/429610695/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
