      "created_at": "2018-10-14T13:53:12Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-14T13:53:12Z",
      "body": "@pemaier To second what @osworx said. There is no need to have a \"agree\" checkbox for a contact form, as long as you are only using the data to action and reply to their request (If you were adding their details to a mailing list that would be a totally different matter). The legal basis will be contract or maybe even legitimate interest (if you can justify it). To have a \"agree\" checkbox would imply you are gaining consent, which the rules for are not easy to implement (see my previous comment).\r\n\r\nA simple notice is what's need in most cases.\r\n> For information about what we do with personal data see our **privacy notice**.\r\n\r\nI would even go as far to say the \"agree\" checkboxes on registering an account are not required. See the \"Create an account\" example on the ICO website.\r\nhttps://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/guide-to-the-general-data-protection-regulation-gdpr/the-right-to-be-informed/how-should-we-provide-privacy-information-to-individuals/#how4",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
